From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:18:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gpu_display: share scanout conversion and blit

Use one Wayland input, scaling and reconnect implementation for all
Gunyah guests. Bring the CPU pixel layouts and fenced Wayland blit into
the current display interface, and route simplefb through its frame copy.
Keep the existing key-release-on-leave implementation for every window.

Adapt the display changes from Droid-VM/crosvm 8883a20c2, 6455258e8
and 8b754f606, plus GunyahVM 67df353bbbe9 and 3b9c88872409.
GunyahVM d8218a2 duplicates the key-release handling already carried by
the display reconnect change, so it needs no second implementation.

TEST=ARM64 release build; gpu_display tests (11 passed)
TEST=11 generated Linux launch profiles parse; application pytest passes
BUG=None

Purpose: Share scanout conversion and blit.
Origin: Droid-VM/crosvm and GunyahVM commits cited above.
Upstream-Status: Downstream GunyahVM carry; not submitted to crosvm upstream.
